# Goal 14: Fix logb (double) — subnormal exponent off by 1

## Function
`logb` (double)

## Source files
- C: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/logbd.c
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs

## Problem
logb(0x0.0000000000001p-1022) = -0x1.0ccp+10 (-1075, Rust) vs -0x1.0c8p+10 (-1074, C)

The smallest subnormal double has exponent -1074 (since the mantissa has 52 bits and minimum biased exponent is -1022, so -1022 - 52 = -1074). The Rust implementation returns -1075, off by 1.

## What needs to change
Compare Rust logb against C logbd.c. The subnormal normalization loop or leading-zero count is off by one. Check whether the counting starts from the wrong bit position or the loop has an off-by-one.

## Success Criteria
- `logb 0x0.0000000000001p-1022` = `-0x1.0c8p+10` (-1074, bitwise exact)
- All other logb tests continue to pass
